{{also|hochštapler}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Thieves' argot; from ''[[Stappler]]'' "[[beggar]]", not related to ''[[stapeln]]''. ''Hochstapler'' means a beggar acting like he is originally high class, but in a dire situation.

